    "coverage_corrections": [
      "DLL names remain the same matchers; raised to notable runtime references, without asserting a GCJ Java wrapper. Broad framework suppressors intentionally no longer inherit compiler DLL references: these do not establish an application framework. Exact BusyBox consumers were updated.",
      "Source-map name detection requires a basename suffix, includes mjs/cjs, and rejects .js.map.backup or directory-only occurrences. Exact consumers were updated.",
      "Raw x86 third-argument 0x40 observation is an operand fact; the memory-protection composite now also requires VirtualProtect import, and no longer maps to reflective code loading.",
      "C rename has a canonical structured symbol matcher on PE/DLL; text fallback no longer duplicates imports or establishes the Windows rename umbrella alone.",
      "popen uses generic T1059/E1059 across Unix and Windows; CreateThread no longer claims shared-module loading.",
      "MagicString distribution source maps gain a content-corroborated identity without a scanned basename requirement.",
      "Updated the ReDoc source-map fixture expectation from the former structured-format directory to the exact source-map suffix trait; the required observation is preserved at its corrected home."
